{
  "_comment": "Scoped permissions for the UNATTENDED weekly doc/IaC drift audit (doc-drift-audit.sh runs `claude -p --settings THIS --permission-mode default`, replacing --dangerously-skip-permissions). Posture: read anything / write docs+READMEs+CLAUDE.md only / mutate nothing but a GitHub workflow_dispatch. The DENY list is the real safety net (deny beats allow, and beats any other settings source). Empirically: in headless `default` mode a Bash command matching neither the safe-read list nor an allow rule is hard-DENIED (no human to prompt); `$(...)` substitution and `VAR=x cmd` env-prefixes are rejected by the matcher, so the audit runs commands stepwise and routes secret+curl ops through infra/devbox/audit-helpers.sh (SOPS_AGE_KEY_FILE is exported by the wrapper, so plain `sops -d <file>` works). Residual risk (intrinsic to the job): `sops -d` reads any encrypted file, and `curl` can issue any HTTP method — both low blast-radius (the dispatch PAT is Actions:write-only). See doc-drift-audit-prompt.md + infra/devbox/README.md.",
